#. type: Title ==
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitformat-index.txt:389
#, no-wrap
msgid "Index Entry Offset Table"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitformat-index.txt:395
msgid ""
"The Index Entry Offset Table (IEOT) is used to help address the CPU cost of "
"loading the index by enabling multi-threading the process of converting "
"cache entries from the on-disk format to the in-memory format.  The "
"signature for this extension is { 'I', 'E', 'O', 'T' }."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitformat-index.txt:399
msgid "32-bit version (currently 1)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitformat-index.txt:401
msgid "A number of index offset entries each consisting of:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitformat-index.txt:404
msgid ""
"32-bit offset from the beginning of the file to the first cache entry in "
"this block of entries."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitformat-index.txt:406
msgid "32-bit count of cache entries in this block"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitformat-index.txt:407
#, no-wrap
msgid "Sparse Directory Entries"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitformat-index.txt:418
msgid ""
"When using sparse-checkout in cone mode, some entire directories within the "
"index can be summarized by pointing to a tree object instead of the entire "
"expanded list of paths within that tree. An index containing such entries is "
"a \"sparse index\". Index format versions 4 and less were not implemented "
"with such entries in mind. Thus, for these versions, an index containing "
"sparse directory entries will include this extension with signature { 's', "
"'d', 'i', 'r' }. Like the split-index extension, tools should avoid "
"interacting with a sparse index unless they understand this extension."
msgstr ""

